<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sijilmasa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sijilmasa was a medieval trading city in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tafilalt">Tafilalt</a> oasis of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> and a northern terminus of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">trans-Saharan gold</a> trade. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> captured it in the early 1050s, gaining control over the gold trade. Its first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahdi">Mahdi</a>, was proclaimed after being retrieved from Sijilmasa in 909.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sijilmasa.jpg" alt="Sijilmasa" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loonybad · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1886608-the_ruins_of_Sijilmassa-Rissani.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
